Original commit body from 0192d95283bdd91e76a9b328fa1c61f72aaf5c9d:

Per ADR-0036 D1a the path slot is the one colon-TOLERANT slot -- `dart:io`,
`std::io` -- so `parts[1]` is a truncation wherever it is used on one. Four
such reads in verify_claims and io_boundary now go through
`ir.symbol_path_slot`.

The name-slot reads behind the disclosure a reader actually SEES now go through
`ir.symbol_name_slot`: the untyped-receiver caveat had been naming
`writeToFile` for the Objective-C selector `writeToFile:atomically:` -- a
method that does not exist, which is worse than naming nothing because a reader
can act on it and find no such call. That is WI-nakut's objc symptom.

THIS CHANGE WAS REDUCED MID-FLIGHT AFTER ITS PREMISE WAS REFUTED, and the
refutation came from the suite rather than from review. The first cut asserted
that "only parts[0] and parts[-1] are colon-free by the grammar" and added a
shrink-only gate over ~13 positional name-slot reads. THAT PREMISE IS FALSE:
ADR-0036 Ruling 1 makes the NAME slot colon-free BY RULE --
`sanitize_id_name_segment` folds `:` to `.` and `make_symbol_id` applies it to
every name slot (WI-sikar) -- so `parts[-2]` is correct on a well-formed id and
those reads are the grammar being relied on, not defects.
`test_id_format_validator_names_the_name_slot_colon_not_the_span` failed and
said so. The gate and its baseline are gone.

ONE PART OF THAT FIRST CUT WAS AN ACTIVE REGRESSION AND WAS REVERTED.
Span-anchoring `validate_symbol_id_format` made it locate the span CORRECTLY ON
A MALFORMED ID, so an id with a colon in its name slot parsed clean and the
`colon_in_name_slot` diagnosis fell silent -- a diagnosis INV-dulah paid a real
investigation to get right, and a validator going quiet is the false-clean
direction. Both validators keep `parts[-3]` deliberately, now with a comment
saying why.

THE ROOT CAUSE OF THE OBJC SYMPTOM IS A PRODUCER DEFECT AT ONE LINE, not a
parsing defect at fifteen. `make_unresolved_edge` (analyze/base.py:880) builds
its dst with a raw f-string and never applies the sanitiser -- exactly what
spec_validator's own error message warns against ("Use make_symbol_id(...)
rather than constructing IDs with f-strings"). Measured on Mantle (31 .m
files): the resulting empty name feeds `_dedupe_key`, so 80 distinct selectors
collapse to 17, 268 of 319 external dsts are nameless, and one node absorbs 49
edges across 134 call sites.

THE OBVIOUS FIX IS NOT OBVIOUSLY RIGHT, so it is filed rather than decided.
Sanitising at the producer restores the grammar and reproduces all 80 distinct
names (verified) -- but 107 of the 128 primitives in io_primitives/objc.yaml
carry a colon in their NAME (`fileExistsAtPath:`, `writeToFile:atomically:`),
so it would break catalogue matching unless the qualified index registers the
folded form too. Restore the grammar at the producer, or amend the grammar to
admit the colon: both arms need an ADR edit, and both are on INV-divuf with the
measurements.

`_span_token_index` is extracted as a plain DRY refactor -- the two chokepoints
carried an identical copy of the span-locating loop -- and changes no
behaviour.

